    "slug": "somalia-schedules-september-30-polls-for-galmudug-and-hirshabelle",
    "summary": "Somalia's electoral commission has set September 30, 2026, for local council and parliamentary elections in Galmudug and Hirshabelle, following a court ruling that annulled previous results in Galmudug. Separate timelines were released on Tuesday for both federal member states.",
    "content": "Somalia's Independent National Electoral and Boundaries Commission has announced that local council and parliamentary elections in the federal member states of Galmudug and Hirshabelle will take place on September 30, 2026. The announcement, made on Tuesday, follows separate electoral timelines released for each state, marking a key step in the country's ongoing regional election process.\n\nThe decision comes after Somalia's Supreme Court annulled the previous election results in Galmudug, necessitating fresh polls. The court's ruling was a response to challenges against the validity of earlier outcomes. The new dates are intended to ensure compliance with the legal ruling and to allow for a new electoral cycle in the affected regions.\n\nLocal and parliamentary elections are part of Somalia's broader efforts to establish stable governance across its federal states. Galmudug and Hirshabelle are two of the five federal member states, each with its own regional administration. The timing of these polls is crucial for maintaining political continuity and addressing any disputes that arose from the earlier rounds.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, these elections carry significant implications. Diaspora communities often maintain strong ties to their regions of origin, and the outcome of these polls can influence clan dynamics, resource allocation, and development priorities in areas where many have family connections. A transparent electoral process is seen as a foundation for long-term stability and investment, which are of direct concern to diaspora members considering business or humanitarian involvement in Somalia.\n\nThe commission has stated that it will work with regional authorities to ensure that the elections are conducted smoothly and according to the announced schedule. Observers will be monitoring the process to guarantee fairness and credibility, aiming to restore public confidence in the electoral system.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/09/01/somalia-sets-september-30-for-galmudug-hirshabelle-elections/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=somalia-sets-september-30-for-galmudug-hirshabelle-elections",
